{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396761-3rd-edition-melee-vs-ma-question","id":1396761,"title":"3rd edition Melee vs MA question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-15T17:32:56-07:00","id":1396761,"title":"3rd edition Melee vs MA question","content":"Our group is doing some serious chatting about what to do when we are done with Curse of Strahd, and we've settled on Exalted 3rd edition. Our GM is an old Exalted hand, and this will be his first chance to run the new edition. We've all picked our castes, and I've ended up as the party Dawn, which I'm pretty happy about. Now, as a Dawn, I gotta kick some sort of butt, and I've put together the concept of a sword-master princess with dreams of grandeur and empire.<br /> <br /> But to my real question. I'm torn between building her with Shining Point in the Void Martial Arts style (the iaijitsu style) or with normal old Melee charms. I know that both choices have their merits and downsides, and I'd like the opinion of some others, especially people who have actually played the system. I know the Void style is a bit more limited, but very flavorful and &quot;special&quot; (she's a princess, and there's every chance her family wanted her trained in a style that was a little unique compared to more traditional swordsmanship), and Melee is broad and straightforward, but it's also more general.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26235-charade","name":"Charade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T18:16:22-07:00","id":1396769,"title":"","content":"Well melee is just better all around, it has more tricks, waaaay better defenses, and is a bit more generic, so it's easier to flavour however you want. On the other hand you can take all of Single Point style right off chargen if you want, and still have six charms leftover for whatever else you're interested in. That lets you just take those 9 charms and study them really well to see how they work and when you want to use them. Plus it has flavour built into it that you don't need to even think of with it's single doom strike flash abilities and stuff.<br /> <br /> Flipside, you could take all your charms in melee and spend the next 50 sessions buying only melee charms and you still won't have them all. It's also a lot more simple and straightforward. It has charms like &quot;Ignore all penalties to your defense.&quot; and &quot;add up to 5 Withering damage for up to 5 motes.&quot; whereas Single Point has charms like &quot;Roll in your sword as a separate character into this combat, with these specific restrictions on what it does and how it works, and when it's crashed you get forced to drop your Form, except if you're a Solar where you stay in the form but the sword vanishes from the initiative track for 3 turns...&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again as an MA Supernal you get access to EVERY Martial Art, so if you wanted to mix styles with your slashing sword you can pick up Steel Devil Style, or even just branch out into other styles so that you have options for when you're armed with your sword, and also insanely deadly if you get disarmed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, whatever one you take you'll be able to kill pretty much anything at your leisure, so you don't really have to worry about one being a &quot;trap&quot; option which will eventually mean you suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T05:36:07-07:00","id":1396851,"title":"","content":"3E's signature Dawn is Volfer. He's the default character showing you how to build a Dawn and what a Dawn can do.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1367860#post1367860\">A reasonably optimized Single Point Solar can kill Volfer in one round.</a><br /> <br /> In fact, power up Volfer with permenant Yozi venom, and tie the Single Point stylist down by giving them half-Willpower and not letting them flare their anima... and Single Point kills Volfer flawlessly in four rounds.<br /> <br /> The Exalted are crazy strong. You are not meant to optimize them. You are meant to play a fun and flavorful concept that interests you.<br /> <br /> If Single Point interests you, you should play it.<br /> <br /> It is MORE THAN strong enough to work for you in regular play, even if you don't optimize.<br /> <br /> That said, it's worth talking to the ST and other players about how much combat you will have and how good everyone will be expected to be at combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T06:02:00-07:00","id":1396854,"title":"","content":"I agree with John; as the party's Dawn, chances are whether you're okay for a Dawn, good for a Dawn, or broken strong for a Dawn, you're setting the bar for the top level of combat power in your group. So I wouldn't worry too much about whether you're powerful enough. If you take Physical attributes primary, your combat ability at 5, and supernal in that combat ability... you're going to be really good at combat.<br /> <br /> If you've not played Ex3 before, I'd recommend Melee because it's much simpler and covers more bases. But that depends how good you are at mechanics. If you're good at mechanics Single Point should be fine.<br /> <br /> I'd say, at the end of the day, it's probably fine to think &quot;how do I imagine her sword-fighting to be like&quot;, and if it's Iajitsu with a katana, take Single Point, if not, take Melee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T06:37:20-07:00","id":1396856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396761-3rd-edition-melee-vs-ma-question?p=1396854#post1396854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with John; as the party's Dawn, chances are whether you're okay for a Dawn, good for a Dawn, or broken strong for a Dawn, you're setting the bar for the top level of combat power in your group. So I wouldn't worry too much about whether you're powerful enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t necessarily say that. If Charade\u2019s group is anything like basically every group I\u2019ve ever been in, everyone is going to take combat ability 5, with a specialty, with physical at least secondary, and 2-3 combat charms minimum. Also likely artifact weapons and armor even if they\u2019re Solars and have a hard time using them. If you\u2019re the Dawn and you do that but instead you take 4-5 combat charms, you won\u2019t feel like your party\u2019s Dawn, you\u2019ll just be the Zenith except a tiny bit better at fighting. In that group if you actually want to feel like the Dawn who\u2019s head and shoulders above your circle mates at fighting the way the Eclipse is head and shoulders over everyone else at sailing, then you\u2019re going to have to go pretty hard into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T06:54:53-07:00","id":1396859,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider as you have stated that you'd like a rarer style of combat...is that single point is rare and unique but not among it's adherents. Martial arts students taught the same style will look relatively the same. After all you're learning the same katas utilizing the same weapons, especially in single point which only uses slashing swords and their artifact equivalent the reaper daiklave. Melee charms, all exalted type charms, are no longer sorceries as they were in the past editions, but are now natural extensions of your characters abilities.<br /> <br /> So a spear fighter with the same charms as a sword fighter would still look differently in a real fight. So your sword princess can have whatever unique style she likes because of what type of sword you chose and how you portray her fighting with it. Martial arts charms on the other hand are not natural abilities of the exalted but rather deliberate shapings of essence more akin to sorcery. A single point swordsman looks differently from a melee swordsman, but not so much a another single point swordsman. Two melee using reaper daiklave wielders might look completely different based on their style descriptions, their stunts. Not to mention melees bigger tree allows for a greater divergence of supernatural skill, which can easily help distinguish your characters style. At least that is my belief, hope it helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T06:58:26-07:00","id":1396860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396761-3rd-edition-melee-vs-ma-question?p=1396856#post1396856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn\u2019t necessarily say that. If Charade\u2019s group is anything like basically every group I\u2019ve ever been in, everyone is going to take combat ability 5, with a specialty, with physical at least secondary, and 2-3 combat charms minimum. Also likely artifact weapons and armor even if they\u2019re Solars and have a hard time using them. If you\u2019re the Dawn and you do that but instead you take 4-5 combat charms, you won\u2019t feel like your party\u2019s Dawn, you\u2019ll just be the Zenith except a tiny bit better at fighting. In that group if you actually want to feel like the Dawn who\u2019s head and shoulders above your circle mates at fighting the way the Eclipse is head and shoulders over everyone else at sailing, then you\u2019re going to have to go pretty hard into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't quite the same with the games I've played. Most Solars do have a combat ability at 5, but not artefact equipment.<br /> <br /> Still, it raises a good point. Charade, what is your group like? Is everyone going to be built for combat and kitted out with artefacts, or do you think not really?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T07:42:34-07:00","id":1396863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396761-3rd-edition-melee-vs-ma-question?p=1396860#post1396860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't quite the same with the games I've played. Most Solars do have a combat ability at 5, but not artefact equipment.<br /> <br /> Still, it raises a good point. Charade, what is your group like? Is everyone going to be built for combat and kitted out with artefacts, or do you think not really?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's hard to say, for sure. I'm pretty far ahead of the rest of my group as far as character conceptualization, for the simple two reasons of 1. I'm the most familiar with Exalted outside of the GM and 2. I just reused a character concept from an Exalted game that never really took off.<br /> <br /> I know for a fact that our Zenith is going to be a right bruiser, the player has been taking hard looks at Brawl charms and White Reaper MA and trying to figure out which they want to do. If I had to guess I'd say that the Night will likely be more ninja-like than not, since that is something the player likes to do. The Twilight and the Eclipse I couldn't say, since they are the least familiar with the setting and are the furthest behind on character creation (which is fine, we're still doing Strahd right now).<br /> <br /> The Twilight has talked about playing a Mad Scientist of some flavor, which could mean anything, but I suspect the Eclipse won't be a combat beast. She plays our cleric in Strahd and is patently not aggressive. Which isn't to say her cleric isn't MVP in most battles.<br /> <br /> I've also considered combining the two fighting styles, melee and Shining Point, but I worry I won't have the dots for that as a starting character and also be able to create a somewhat rounded character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26235-charade","name":"Charade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T07:48:07-07:00","id":1396864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396761-3rd-edition-melee-vs-ma-question?p=1396863#post1396863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also considered combining the two fighting styles, melee and Shining Point, but I worry I won't have the dots for that as a starting character and also be able to create a somewhat rounded character.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should be basically a non-issue. If you have maxed out 5 in both abilities it takes 20% of your starting ability dots, and 25% of your bonus points. So basically you max out both Single Point and Melee and you still have 80% of your character to do whatever else you want with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T07:53:28-07:00","id":1396868,"title":"","content":"The bigger issue is charm selection, but that's also simple as you'll want defensive options to shore up single point's weaknesses. The offensive charms aren't necessary for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T07:55:06-07:00","id":1396869,"title":"","content":"Just be careful combining them because you can only attack with one at a time and parry with one at a time. You may end up with identical ratings of course, but you can't combine the charms, or use Melee charms with the extra attack from Single Point's form.<br /> <br /> It is a strong combo though, as you can use Single Point for attack and Melee for defence. Otherwise you'd probably want Dodge or Resistance for defence anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T07:58:37-07:00","id":1396870,"title":"","content":"Dodge is eventually a great option, especially long game where you can potentially crash an enemy and strip his initiative with a successful dodge. Whis is perfect for fights where you can't just one and done it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:34:50-07:00","id":1396878,"title":"","content":"Also as a heads up especially to your Storyteller, that kind of thinking and optimization will make a good 60-70% of the antagonist chapter nearly worthless. Most antagonists in Exalted have 8 or fewer dice to attack, and the ones that have more often have very weak damage on those attacks, while simultaneously having weak to middling soak. If every characer is kitted out for combat, especially if one person is using the potent Single Point + Melee combo, it will be extremely difficult to find any kind of satisfying fight using the printed antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:41:05-07:00","id":1396881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396761-3rd-edition-melee-vs-ma-question?p=1396878#post1396878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also as a heads up especially to your Storyteller, that kind of thinking and optimization will make a good 60-70% of the antagonist chapter nearly worthless. Most antagonists in Exalted have 8 or fewer dice to attack, and the ones that have more often have very weak damage on those attacks, while simultaneously having weak to middling soak. If every characer is kitted out for combat, especially if one person is using the potent Single Point + Melee combo, it will be extremely difficult to find any kind of satisfying fight using the printed antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a bit of a worry, because I want people to have fun and I don't want to ruin the experience for anyone. That being said, our GM has been playing Exalted for a long time. He doesn't have a ton of 3rd edition experience, but I trust his ability to build some antagonists that will go head-to-head with us, in a number of different ways. I'm definitely leaning towards Melee for Defense and Single Point for attack right now, but I may have to build it out and see what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26235-charade","name":"Charade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T09:51:14-07:00","id":1396892,"title":"","content":"If he has a lot of 2e experience this kind of thing will probably be familiar to him. It\u2019s a much easier problem to deal with in Ex3 than 2e. At least in third edition you can take that 30% of antagonists who can be useful and piles them on in great numbers and with extreme environmental effects. It can still be fun, but my first four or five Ex3 campaigns were plagued by trying to use creatures with 6-8 dice attacks to hit PCs with a base defense of 7, and then trying to get past 13 soak with 11 withering damage. <br /> <br /> Also the book makes no distinctions in the antagonist chapter about what\u2019s actually supposed to be an antagonist, and what\u2019s just put there to act as mounts/familiars for players, or animal shapes for Lunars. So you get things like the Stegodon style Siege Lizard, which looks like it\u2019s supposed to be an antagonist to fight, but it ends up being there for players to take as a pet instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T20:10:02-07:00","id":1397212,"title":"","content":"on a straight up 1 v 1 with the right charms melee destroys without the other person even having a chance to act","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T00:58:23-07:00","id":1397250,"title":"","content":"A couple of things to keep in mind when making your choice between Single Point and Melee:<br /> <br /> 1: Single Point is an amazing offence, like probably one of the best offensive charmsets in the game. It has basically no defense. If you want to pick up some melee parry charms or dodge charms you will be nearly invincible. That may or may not be a good thing depending on the game and players. I have seen at least one player rebuild their character away from using Single Point style because with a few charms they were trivializing the efforts of a less optimized Dawn caste (newer player) and the martial artist had been an eclipse who wanted to be competent at combat, but not better than the dawn.<br /> <br /> 2: As a Martial Arts Style Single Point can be bought with solar XP as you go along. That means if you go Single Point you could well devote all of your regular xp to non-combat things to be very well rounded charm wise without sacrificing combat power. Your overall skill and attributes will be a bit lower, but in my experience that is less important than getting the charms you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}